## 2. Relative Spectral Phases

On the unramified spectral locus, write a Hermitian rank-three endomorphism as

\[
X=
\begin{pmatrix}
d_0 & z_{01} & \overline{z_{20}}\\
\overline{z_{01}} & d_1 & z_{12}\\
z_{20} & \overline{z_{12}} & d_2
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Changing the phases of the three eigenline frames acts by

\[
z_{ij}\longmapsto
e^{i(\theta_i-\theta_j)}z_{ij}.
\]

The common central phase cancels. The effective phase group is therefore

\[
T^3/U(1)_{\rm central}\simeq T^2.
\]

This is the relative-phase datum which the shared central circle does not
remove.

## 3. Exact Invariant Ring

Put

\[
r_{12}=|z_{12}|^2,\qquad
r_{20}=|z_{20}|^2,\qquad
r_{01}=|z_{01}|^2
\]

and

\[
t=z_{12}z_{20}z_{01}=u+iv.
\]

The relative-phase invariant real polynomial ring is generated by

\[
d_0,d_1,d_2,\quad
r_{12},r_{20},r_{01},\quad
u,v
\]

with the relation

\[
u^2+v^2=r_{12}r_{20}r_{01}.
\]

### Proof

Represent a monomial in the oriented entries \(z_{ij}\) and
\(\overline{z_{ij}}=z_{ji}\) by a directed multigraph on three vertices.
Its torus weight vanishes exactly when the incoming and outgoing degrees
agree at every vertex. Such a graph is Eulerian and decomposes into directed
cycles.

On three vertices, every directed cycle decomposes into:

- the three two-cycles \(z_{ij}z_{ji}=|z_{ij}|^2\);
- the positive three-cycle \(t\);
- the reverse three-cycle \(\bar t\).

This proves generation. Hermitian conjugacy gives

\[
t\bar t=r_{12}r_{20}r_{01},
\]

which is the displayed real relation.

There are eight real generators and one relation. The generic quotient
therefore has real dimension

\[
8-1=7.
\]

This is the elementary three-vertex instance of the cycle-generator
principle in quiver invariant theory.

## 4. The Missing Orientation Coordinate

Even sheet permutations preserve the orientation of the triangle and send
\(t\) to \(t\). Odd permutations reverse it and send

\[
t\longmapsto\bar t.
\]

Consequently

\[
u\longmapsto u,\qquad
v\longmapsto {\rm sign}(\sigma)v.
\]

The imaginary triangle component is a pseudoscalar in the sheet sign
representation. Equivalently, on the regular locus the missing coordinate is
the triangle phase

\[
e^{i\phi}
=
\frac{z_{12}z_{20}z_{01}}
{|z_{12}z_{20}z_{01}|}.
\]

The existing shared determinant line has the correct sign character to carry
the orientation parity of \(v\). This does not select the value of \(\phi\),
identify it with time, or prove that the triangle-phase circle is the shared
central circle.

## 5. Linear Rank-Six No-Go

As a real \(T^2\)-representation,

\[
{\rm Herm}(3)
=D\oplus R_{12}\oplus R_{20}\oplus R_{01},
\]

where \(D\simeq\mathbb R^3\) is torus-trivial and each \(R_{ij}\) is a
two-dimensional nonzero-weight rotation plane.

The three root planes have distinct torus weights. A torus-stable real
subspace is therefore a sum of weight planes and a subspace of \(D\).
The sheet group acts transitively on the three root planes, so an
\(S_3\)-stable choice contains either all three or none.

The only rank-six candidate is consequently

\[
R_{12}\oplus R_{20}\oplus R_{01}.
\]

Its \(S_3\) character on identity, transposition and three-cycle is

\[
(6,0,0)
=
\chi_{\bf1}+\chi_{\rm sign}+2\chi_{\rm std}.
\]

The selected root-stack carrier has character

\[
(6,2,0)
=
2\chi_{\bf1}+2\chi_{\rm std}.
\]

The characters differ. Hence:

> There is no \(T^2\rtimes S_3\)-equivariant linear rank-six subspace of
> \({\rm Herm}(3)\) isomorphic to \(W_{\rm fin}\).

This excludes the old direct-subspace route. It does not exclude a nonlinear
symbol.

## 6. Intrinsic Nonlinear Strain Symbol

Define

\[
\Phi_{\rm strain}(X)
=
\left(
d_0,d_1,d_2,
|z_{12}|^2,|z_{20}|^2,|z_{01}|^2
\right).
\]

This map is:

- invariant under all relative eigenline phases;
- equivariant under the sheet permutation group;
- valued in two permutation copies;
- independent of a choice of real ray inside any complex root plane.

It is a semialgebraic cone-valued map, not a linear projector.

The complete invariant quotient is seven-dimensional. The map
\(\Phi_{\rm strain}\) forgets exactly the triangle phase. This is the lawful
meaning of the six-dimensional strain shadow.

### Regular Differential

At a point with all three edge amplitudes nonzero, \(J=d\Phi_{\rm strain}\)
has rank six. At the exact witness

\[
z_{12}=z_{20}=z_{01}=1,
\]

use the coordinate order

\[
(d_0,d_1,d_2,
\Re z_{12},\Im z_{12},
\Re z_{20},\Im z_{20},
\Re z_{01},\Im z_{01}).
\]

The kernel of \(J\) is three-dimensional. Two directions are infinitesimal
relative-phase gauge transformations. The third changes the
gauge-invariant triangle phase while preserving all three edge norms.

Thus

\[
\ker J
=
\mathfrak t_{\rm relative}^2
\oplus\mathbb R_{\rm orientation}.
\]

If an edge amplitude vanishes, the rank drops. Such points belong to lower
orbit strata and require tangent-cone or root-stack analysis. They are not
silently included in the regular theorem.

## 7. The Correct Effective Hessian

Let \(H_Q\) be the positive gauge-fixed physical Hessian on the orthogonal
complement of its declared harmonic kernel, and let

\[
G_Q=H_Q^{-1}
\]

be its same-source reduced Green operator.

Extend \(J=d\Phi_{\rm strain}\) by zero over the physical fields not read by
the strain symbol. Define

\[
C_{\rm strain}=J G_QJ^*.
\]

If \(J\) has full rank on the declared regular target and
\(C_{\rm strain}\) is positive, define

\[
H_{\rm strain}
=
\left(JG_QJ^*\right)^{-1}.
\]

### Variational Proof

For a declared symbol variation \(y\), minimize

\[
\frac12\langle x,H_Qx\rangle
\]

over all physical variations satisfying

\[
Jx=y.
\]

The Lagrange equations give

\[
x_{\min}
=
G_QJ^*
\left(JG_QJ^*\right)^{-1}y.
\]

Substitution yields

\[
\min_{Jx=y}
\frac12\langle x,H_Qx\rangle
=
\frac12
\left\langle
y,
\left(JG_QJ^*\right)^{-1}y
\right\rangle.
\]

This is the quotient or shorted Hessian. It integrates out:

- the two relative-phase gauge directions;
- the triangle-orientation direction forgotten by the strain symbol;
- every other physical field coupled through the full rank-102 Green
  operator.

No complementary basis or cutoff is selected.

### Presentation Independence

Under a unitary source presentation change \(R\),

\[
H_Q'=RH_QR^*,\qquad
G_Q'=RG_QR^*,\qquad
J'=JR^*.
\]

Therefore

\[
J'G_Q'J'^*=JG_QJ^*.
\]

The effective symbol Hessian is independent of the Cech embedding, local
eigenline phases and source basis.

If the physical operator is treated at a spectral parameter \(z\), the same
construction is applied to the reduced resolvent of \(H_Q-z\). The present
positive-Hodge statement does not promote an indefinite action Hessian
without its declared domain.

## 8. TT Reynolds Reduction

Let

\[
P_{\rm Haar}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
\frac13{\bf1}{\bf1}^T&0\\
0&\frac13{\bf1}{\bf1}^T
\end{pmatrix},
\qquad
Q_{\rm TT}=I-P_{\rm Haar}.
\]

Then

\[
{\rm rank}(P_{\rm Haar})=2,\qquad
{\rm rank}(Q_{\rm TT})=4.
\]

The two removed directions are the trivial sheet and edge modes. This makes
the comparison compatible with the trace-free physical visible adjoint:
only the two standard representations are compared.

The same-source physical TT covariance must first satisfy

\[
[C_{\rm TT},\rho_{\rm TT}(\sigma)]=0
\qquad\text{for every }\sigma\in S_3.
\]

This is a physical structural check. It does not follow merely because the
symbol map is \(S_3\)-equivariant. Once it holds, the real Schur lemma gives

\[
C_{\rm TT}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
a&c\\
c&b
\end{pmatrix}
\otimes I_{\rm std}.
\]

Its effective Hessian is

\[
H_{\rm TT}^{\rm eff}
=
\frac1{ab-c^2}
\begin{pmatrix}
b&-c\\
-c&a
\end{pmatrix}
\otimes I_{\rm std}.
\]

The selected finite Reynolds target is

\[
H_{\rm fin}^{\rm TT}
=
\kappa_{\rm fin}I_2\otimes I_{\rm std}.
\]

Therefore equality up to one positive overall normalization holds exactly
when

\[
c=0,\qquad a=b>0.
\]

Then

\[
\kappa_{\rm fin}=\frac1a
\]

in covariance normalization.

Without an additional physical symmetry, the exit would contain one
structural covariance check, two dimensionless equality checks and one
already declared action scale. A single scale cannot repair a nonzero
\(S_3\) commutator, \(c\ne0\), or \(a\ne b\).

The certificate verifies both:

```text
