    -> effective Hessian [[3/5,-1/5],[-1/5,2/5]]
    -> no overall-scale match;

isotropic covariance 2 I2
    -> effective Hessian (1/2) I2
    -> exact Reynolds match with kappa_fin=1/2.
```

Both are proof witnesses, not physical q79 values.

## 9. Shorted Symmetry Inheritance

The adjacent finite root-stack theorem supplies the exact target
quarter-turn

\[
J_{DE}(d,e)=(-e,d),
\qquad
J_{DE}=
\begin{pmatrix}
0&-I_3\\
I_3&0
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

It obeys

\[
J_{DE}^2=-I_6,\qquad
J_{DE}^TJ_{DE}=I_6,\qquad
[J_{DE},\rho(\sigma)]=0
\]

for every \(\sigma\in S_3\).

Here \(J_{DE}\) acts on the linearized strain tangent carrier at the selected
background. It is not asserted to be a global automorphism of the
semialgebraic cone \((d_i,|z_{ij}|^2)\), which it does not generally preserve.

Now let \(U\) be a selected same-source action on the reduced physical
carrier and \(V\) its action on the strain tangent. Require \(U\) to preserve
the gauge-fixed harmonic-complement domain and either fix the background or
canonically transport its tangent fiber. Assume

\[
UG_QU^*=G_Q,\qquad JU=VJ.
\]

Then shorting inherits the symmetry:

\[
\begin{aligned}
V C_{\rm strain}V^*
&=VJG_QJ^*V^*\\
&=JUG_QU^*J^*\\
&=JG_QJ^*\\
&=C_{\rm strain}.
\end{aligned}
\]

This is exact and basis-free. It applies equally to the inverse effective
Hessian on the regular image.

On the \(S_3\)-covariant TT sector, write

\[
C_{\rm TT}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
a&c\\
c&b
\end{pmatrix}
\otimes I_{\rm std}.
\]

Commutation with the multiplicity quarter-turn gives

\[
\left[
\begin{pmatrix}
a&c\\
c&b
\end{pmatrix},
\begin{pmatrix}
0&-1\\
1&0
\end{pmatrix}
\right]
=
\begin{pmatrix}
2c&b-a\\
b-a&-2c
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Therefore

\[
[C_{\rm TT},J_{DE}]=0
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
c=0,\ a=b.
\]

The certificate computes the commutator map on the three-dimensional
\((a,c,b)\) space. Its rank is two, so the joint \(S_3\)- and
\(J_{DE}\)-invariant TT commutant is exactly one-dimensional, generated by
\(Q_{\rm TT}\).

Consequently the two dimensionless TT equalities are no longer independent
numerical targets. They follow from one typed same-carrier symmetry-lift
theorem. The required physical lift is not promoted here: the finite
root-stack \(J_{DE}\) is known, but its action on the selected nonzero-Chern
HYM/reduced-Green carrier remains open.

